ly on that  is a great thing that helped us and when  we did that we also copied the dimension  data to the cloud so that they can get  the entire data set how to play with  query cost this is very very important  and even now we know we have been seeing  some of the areas where we can improve  in our in our company but what we did  especially with our cloud migration we  have created some alerts early on to  alert us if any query if anybody is  running a query that cost the cost is  exceeding certain limit we'll get an  email or alert so it's like a training  the users to tell them hey you know this  is the query you ran and this query cost  a few thousand dollars and so please be  mindful because you know we had queries  in aware initially when we started  working with bigquery there were users  are now who round the queries worth  $8,000 you may not believe it but that  is true but pretty quickly you know we  were able to you know contain that and  then everybody now is you know able to  run the queries very effectively and  those alerts helped us and even we are  continuously improving on how well you  know we can improve the process and also  our strategy with go-live is a  sequential and that how does a lot  because it gave us momentum you know  once we go live with first business unit  it give us a momentum for the rest of  the groups and had to go alive because  they have seen other people other  business units going live and that  helped you know us and also them so  there's what I would suggest you know if  you have many many brands that's what I  think you can take that approach and as  you have seen oh this is a very very  complex project or many many brands with  a lot of different priorities and we  have a great team and excellent  stakeholders and that is how we were  able to do it and  that's all what we have and thank you  for joining our session today  [Music]
 

